# Web Framework Guide

The web framework is a modular Express.js-like system built on top of the HTTP module.

## Core Files
- [scripts/web/application.lua](mdc:scripts/web/application.lua) - Main application class
- [scripts/web/router.lua](mdc:scripts/web/router.lua) - URL routing implementation

## Middleware Modules
Located in `scripts/web/`:
- [scripts/web/static.lua](mdc:scripts/web/static.lua) - Static file serving
- [scripts/web/views.lua](mdc:scripts/web/views.lua) - Template rendering
- [scripts/web/json.lua](mdc:scripts/web/json.lua) - JSON request/response handling
- [scripts/web/cookie.lua](mdc:scripts/web/cookie.lua) - Cookie parsing/setting
- [scripts/web/formparser.lua](mdc:scripts/web/formparser.lua) - Form data parsing
- [scripts/web/multipart.lua](mdc:scripts/web/multipart.lua) - File upload handling

## Examples
See [examples/app.lua](mdc:examples/app.lua) for a complete application example showing:
- Middleware usage
- Route handling
- Template rendering
- File uploads
- Static file serving

## Documentation
The full web framework documentation is available in [docs/web.md](mdc:docs/web.md)
